an8.13:1.5 | S: He’s bred in the region fine thoroughbreds come from. | T: he is born in the country where other auspicious thoroughbred steeds are born.
an8.13:1.6 | S: Whatever food he’s given, | T: [2] “When given food,
an8.13:1.7 | S: fresh or dry, | T: whether fresh or dried,
an8.13:1.8 | S: he eats carefully, without making a mess. | T: he eats it carefully, without scattering it around.
an8.13:1.9 | S: He’s disgusted by sitting or lying down in excrement or urine. | T: [3] “He feels disgust at sitting or lying down in urine or excrement.
an8.13:1.10 | S: He’s gentle and pleasant to live with, and he doesn’t upset the other horses. | T: [4] “He is composed & easy to live with, and doesn’t harass the other horses.
an8.13:1.11 | S: He openly shows his tricks, bluffs, ruses, and feints to his trainer, | T: [5] “Whatever tricks or deceits or wiles or subterfuges he has, he shows them as they actually are to his trainer,
