an8.13:2.5 | S: coarse or fine, | T: whether coarse or refined,
an8.13:2.6 | S: they eat carefully, without bother. | T: he eats it carefully, without complaining.
an8.13:2.7 | S: They’re disgusted with bad conduct by way of body, speech, or mind, | T: [3] “He feels disgust at bodily misconduct, verbal misconduct, mental misconduct,
